# TeamSync REST API Integration Guide & Endpoints Reference (`apiguide`)

Base URL: http://localhost:8000/api
Authentication Standard: JSON Web Token (JWT) Bearer Authentication
Content-Type: application/json (or multipart/form-data for file uploads)

================================================================================
GLOBAL API REQUEST & RESPONSE CONVENTIONS
================================================================================
Request Headers:
- Content-Type: application/json (or multipart/form-data for uploads)
- Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

HTTP Response Status Codes:
- 200 OK: Request succeeded. Returns requested object or list.
- 201 Created: Resource created successfully.
- 204 No Content: Resource deleted successfully.
- 400 Bad Request: Validation failure or missing fields.
- 401 Unauthorized: Invalid or missing JWT token.
- 403 Forbidden: Insufficient role permissions (e.g. Member creating project).
- 404 Not Found: Targeted resource ID does not exist.

================================================================================
1. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT (/api/auth/)
================================================================================
1.1 USER LOGIN & JWT RETRIEVAL: POST /api/auth/login/
Headers: Content-Type: application/json
Request Body:
  { "username": "admin@teamsync.com", "password": "password123" }
Success Response (200 OK):
  { "access": "eyJhb...", "refresh": "eyJhb...", "user": { "id": 1, "role": "ADMIN", "email": "admin@teamsync.com" } }
Error Response (401 Unauthorized):
  { "detail": "No active account found with the given credentials" }
Error Response (400 Bad Request):
  { "username": ["This field is required."] }

1.2 USER REGISTRATION: POST /api/auth/register/
Headers: Content-Type: application/json
Request Body:
  { "username": "sarahc", "email": "sarah@teamsync.com", "password": "password123", "role": "ADMIN", "department": "Infra" }
Success Response (201 Created):
  { "id": 5, "username": "sarahc", "email": "sarah@teamsync.com", "role": "ADMIN" }
Error Response (400 Bad Request):
  { "username": ["A user with that username already exists."] }

1.3 GET CURRENT USER PROFILE: GET /api/auth/me/
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success Response (200 OK):
  { "id": 1, "username": "admin", "role": "ADMIN", "email": "admin@teamsync.com" }

1.4 LIST USERS / DIRECTORY: GET /api/auth/users/
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success Response (200 OK): Array of User objects.

================================================================================
2. PROJECT MANAGEMENT (/api/projects/)
================================================================================
2.1 LIST PROJECTS & PROGRESS METRICS: GET /api/projects/
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success Response (200 OK):
  [ { "id": 1, "name": "Enterprise Cloud", "progress_percentage": 67, "total_tasks": 3, "completed_tasks": 2 } ]

2.2 CREATE PROJECT: POST /api/projects/ (Admin Only)
Headers: Content-Type: application/json, Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>
Request Body:
  { "name": "Mobile Banking 2.0", "description": "Biometric UI", "status": "ACTIVE", "member_ids": [2, 3] }
Success Response (201 Created):
  { "id": 2, "name": "Mobile Banking 2.0", "progress_percentage": 0, "members": [1, 2, 3] }
Error Response (403 Forbidden):
  { "detail": "You do not have permission to perform this action." }

2.3 ADD PROJECT MEMBER: POST /api/projects/{id}/add_member/ (Admin Only)
Request Body: { "user_id": 4 }
Success Response (200 OK): { "detail": "User added to project successfully.", "project": { ... } }

================================================================================
3. TASK MANAGEMENT & AUDIT TRAIL (/api/tasks/)
================================================================================
3.1 LIST & FILTER TASKS: GET /api/tasks/?project=1&assigned_to_me=true&status=IN_PROGRESS&priority=URGENT
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Success Response (200 OK): Array of Task objects.

3.2 CREATE TASK: POST /api/tasks/ (Admin Only)
Request Body:
  { "title": "Setup OAuth", "project": 1, "assigned_to": 2, "priority": "URGENT", "status": "TODO", "deadline": "2026-09-15T18:00:00Z" }
Success Response (201 Created): { "id": 5, "title": "Setup OAuth", "status": "TODO" }

3.3 UPDATE TASK & DEADLINE AUDIT LOG: PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/
Request Body (Deadline Revision):
  { "deadline": "2026-10-15T18:00:00Z", "deadline_reason": "Scope expansion for MFA compliance." }
Success Response (200 OK): { "id": 5, "deadline": "2026-10-15T18:00:00Z", "deadline_history_count": 1 }
System Behavior: Logs DeadlineHistory, records TaskActivity event, sends email notification to assignee.

3.4 GET TASK DEADLINE HISTORY: GET /api/tasks/{id}/deadline_history/
Success Response (200 OK):
  [ { "previous_deadline": "2026-09-15...", "new_deadline": "2026-10-15...", "reason": "Scope expansion", "changed_by_detail": { ... } } ]

3.5 TASK ACTIVITY HISTORY LOG: GET /api/tasks/{id}/activity_history/
Success Response (200 OK): Chronological audit log of task status updates, deadline revisions, comments, and file attachments.

3.6 TASK COMMENTS: GET / POST /api/tasks/{id}/comments/
POST Body: { "content": "Completed unit testing." }
Success Response (201 Created): { "id": 3, "content": "Completed unit testing.", "author_detail": { ... } }

3.7 TASK FILE ATTACHMENTS: GET / POST /api/tasks/{id}/attachments/
POST Headers: Content-Type: multipart/form-data
POST Form Data: file: <binary file>
Success Response (201 Created): { "id": 1, "file_name": "architecture_spec.pdf", "file_size": 245120 }

3.8 DASHBOARD STATS: GET /api/tasks/dashboard_stats/
Success Response (200 OK):
  { "total_projects": 3, "total_tasks": 5, "completed_tasks": 2, "overall_completion_rate": 40, "total_deadline_changes": 2 }
